            <ArticleTitle>Successful treatment of stutter priapism with an antiandrogen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>167-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recurring periods of prolonged erections in patients with sickle cell disease (stutter priapism) are uncommon, yet troubling sequelae of hemoglobinopathies. Medical or surgical therapy is variably successful in these men. We report a case of stutter priapism successfully treated with an oral antiandrogen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
